    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d59">

                <pb facs="0176" n="60" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg60"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.00/991b.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 210.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-01-16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 16, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I enclose herewith for the information of
                    the Legation a copy of an instruction this day<anchor n="1" xml:id="d59-f1"/>
                    addressed to the Consul General at Hankow regarding the attitude to be assumed
                    by him in his relations with the local revolutionary leaders. In replying to any
                    requests on the part of the American consuls in China for instructions as to the
                        <pb facs="0177" n="61" xml:id="pg61"/> nature of the relations, if any, they
                    may properly enter into with the revolutionary leaders, you should be guided by
                    the general principles embodied in the enclosure to this instruction.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d59-a1.xml" xpointer="d59-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
